{
  "purpose": "Full 12-burst DM-phase crop-window sensitivity (user hypothesis: over-wide window dilutes the shallow DSA phase-coherence surface; tightening toward the on-pulse region gives a more accurate/stable DM).",
  "method": "Reproduce dm-joint-phase-v2 fit_band per burst/band at crop windows [6,8,10,14,20,30] ms (production=30ms fixed). CHIME/DSA DM optima + gaussian_joint tension recomputed at each. Parity with fits.json verified at 30ms for chromatica.",
  "headline": "CHIME DM is crop-ROBUST for all 12 (DM range <=0.007 pc/cm3, median ~0.001, << CHIME sigma ~0.01) -- the strong, uniform result. DSA DM is crop-SENSITIVE (range 0.004-0.119): its shallow phase-coherence surface (low DM leverage at 1.3-1.5 GHz) is diluted by off-pulse fluctuation-frequency noise in a wide window, so the DSA optimum wanders with crop width. The CHIME-DSA tension does NOT move in a single direction with crop (6 bursts increase, 5 decrease, 1 flat between 30ms and +/-4x; changes mostly small) -- so the fixed 30ms window is NOT uniformly inflating tension; rather it makes the DSA cross-check UNSTABLE per-burst. For chromatica specifically the tension does drop (0.89->0.33 at +/-4x). phineas is a GENUINE offset (tension stays 6.5->4.1 sigma). Practical consequence: adopted CHIME-primary DMs are unaffected by crop; only the DSA cross-check is crop-dependent and should use an adaptive window.",
